<title>USA: Paragon CEO confident in dispute with P&amp;G.</title>
<headline>Paragon CEO confident in dispute with P&amp;G.</headline>
<dateline>NORCROSS, Ga. 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Paragon Trade Brands Inc said on Wednesday it is confident of its position as its dispute with Procter &amp; Gamble Co unfolds in U.S. District Court in Delaware.</p>
<p>In the trial, which began Monday, Paragon and Procter &amp; Gamble are suing each other over disposable-diaper patents. Each claims the other has infringed its patents.</p>
<p>Procter &amp; Gamble seeks damages and interest of $101 million; Paragon is asking for damages of about $5 million.</p>
<p>Paragon Chief Executive Bobby Abraham said Procter &amp; Gamble's position was &quot;seriously eviscerated&quot; by a federal judge's decision in an earlier dispute beween P&amp;G and Kimberly-Clark Corp.</p>
<p>		 ((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
